  if (xhr.status === 200) {
    console.log(xhr.responseText); // the response text
  }
};
xhr.send();
```
**Using Fetch API**

The Fetch API is a modern way to make HTTP requests, introduced in JavaScript in 2015. It's a simpler and more intuitive way to make requests.
```javascript
fetch('https://example.com/api/data')
  .then(response => response.text())
  .then(data => console.log(data)); // the response text
```
**Using jQuery**

If you're using the jQuery library, you can use its `ajax` method to make HTTP requests.
```javascript
$.ajax({
  type: 'GET',
  url: 'https://example.com/api/data',
  success: function(data) {
    console.log(data); // the response text
  }
});
```
**Using Axios**

Axios is a popular JavaScript library that provides a simple way to make HTTP requests. You can use it like this:
```javascript
import axios from 'axios';

axios.get('https://example.com/api/data')
  .then(response => console.log(response.data)) // the response data
  .catch(error => console.error(error));
```
